```java
@ParameterizedTest
@CsvSource({"1, true", "0, false", "-1, false", "100, true", "101, false"})
void isValidAge(int age, boolean expected) {
    assertEquals(expected, validator.isValidAge(age));
}
```
JUnit auto-converts the CSV strings to the declared parameter types. Covers: valid range, boundaries (0, 100), below minimum, above maximum. Each row is a separate test. For strings with commas, use `'quote, like this'` or `@CsvSource(delimiterString="|")`.

```java
static Stream<Arguments> provideOrders() {
    return Stream.of(
        Arguments.of(new Order(100, "ELECTRONICS"), new BigDecimal("10.00")),
        Arguments.of(new Order(500, "CLOTHING"), new BigDecimal("25.00"))
    );
}

@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("provideOrders")
void calculateDiscount(Order order, BigDecimal expected) { ... }
```
The method must be `static` (or non-static with PER_CLASS lifecycle). If `@MethodSource` has no value, JUnit looks for a static method with the same name as the test method.
